INT. APPELLATE COURTROOM - DAY

Dark wood, flags, a ceiling of coffered plaster. The gallery is nearly empty. The gavel sits unused.

JUDGE FLORENCE ADEYEMI-HART (60s, black robe, silver locs) presides. Before her, two lawyers at separate lecterns: ATTORNEY GABRIEL SOTOMAYOR-BELL (40s, navy suit) and ATTORNEY NADINE KRAUSE (50s, gray pinstripe).

FLORENCE
Counselors, we've heard enough on the statute.

GABRIEL
Your Honor, one final point.

NADINE
(overlapping)
Your Honor, I object to a final point.

FLORENCE
Let him finish.

GABRIEL
The plaintiff's right of way was established in nineteen-fifty.

NADINE
Established by whom?

GABRIEL
^By the county.

NADINE
^By a county that no longer exists.

Florence raises a hand. Both stop. She adjusts her glasses, glances at a document, and sets it aside.

FLORENCE
Mr. Sotomayor-Bell, sit down.

He sits. Nadine remains standing, stiff.

FLORENCE (CONT'D)
Ms. Krause, you too.

Nadine lowers herself slowly. The courtroom is silent.

FLORENCE (CONT'D)
The court will rule from the bench.

She pauses. Gabriel clasps his hands. Nadine doesn't blink.

FLORENCE (CONT'D)
Affirmed.

A single exhale from the gallery. Gabriel closes his folder. Nadine gathers her papers with great care, and neither looks at the other.
